  "body": "Fixes #1198.  Browsers all behave differently here, and Chrome is\nprobably the most reasonable behavior.  It's also more liberal for\ncolspan (allows up to 8190 instead of 1000 in Firefox/Edge), and agrees\nwith Firefox that rowspan should be allowed up to 65534 (instead of\n65535 in Edge).\n\nFor setting, I followed Firefox because it's the simplest.  Chrome\nconverts negative numbers to 0, and Edge throws in some cases and clamps\nin others.\n\nI think I updated the table algorithm properly, but I don't understand\nit, so please double-check!\n",
